 "summary": "No duplication: the sharp binomial-sum and product-binomial bounds are not stated by the existing coefficient-length bounds (L1Norm.lean) or the absolute-value jet bound (Abv/Taylor.lean), and the roadmap (README.md:1124-1127) explicitly asks for the coarse univariate bound to be derived through `Nat.sum_Icc_choose_mul_pow_le`. `TauCeti.norm_mul_prod_pow_le` fills a real gap: the existing product-norm lemmas assume `NormOneClass`, and the proofs reuse `norm_mul_pow_le`, `norm_nsmul_le` and `hasseDeriv_monomial`.",
